// ╔═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║  zellij LAYOUT — zjstatus status bar (quick task 260820-1kp)        ║
// ╚═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
//
// ── Why a SECOND zellij template, separate from zellij-config.kdl ──────
// zjstatus is not configurable from config.kdl. Measured last session:
// driving it through the `plugins{}` alias block in config.kdl parsed
// clean ("Well defined") and the session rendered ~36k of output, but the
// format string never appeared on screen. Its own docs configure it as a
// `pane { plugin location=... }` inside a LAYOUT, which is a different
// file with a different schema — hence a second template and a second
// contract entry (20 -> 21) rather than more lines in the existing one.
//
// ── output_path is the STATE DIR, not ~/.config/zellij/layouts directly ──
// Same posture as zellij-config.kdl: matugen renders into
// ~/.local/state/theme/ and lib/commit.sh symlinks it to
// ~/.config/zellij/layouts/rice.kdl. The theme engine owns the render;
// commit.sh owns the wiring. Nothing writes into the repo tree.
//
// ── Plugin paths use `file:~/...` on purpose (host-portability) ────────
// A rendered template cannot expand $HOME — matugen has no such keyword —
// so an absolute /home/<user>/ path baked in here would break every other
// machine and the fresh-install gate, the same class of bug the relative
// wallpaper symlink fix closed. Verified against the installed binary
// rather than assumed: zellij 0.44.3 links shellexpand 3.0.0 and carries
// the error string "Failed to shell expand plugin path:", so it shell-
// expands plugin locations and `~` resolves per-host at load time.
//
// ── No reload hook (D-05, inherited) ──────────────────────────────────
// zellij watches its own config; lib/reload.sh stays the sole fan-out
// owner and needs no entry for this file either.
//
// ── NAMED colours, not hex — and this is the load-bearing decision ────
// The bar originally used matugen hex. It rendered correctly but could
// NOT live-re-theme, which breaks this project's core value. Measured
// 2026-08-20: zjstatus's colours are baked into this LAYOUT, and zellij
// reads a layout only when a pane is created. Switching catppuccin ->
// nord and then running `zellij action start-or-reload-plugin` left the
// bar still emitting 24 catppuccin-purple SGR codes and zero nord ones.
// A plugin reload does not re-read layout config; only a new session or
// tab does.
//
// Named colours fix it. zjstatus resolves them to ANSI-16 SGR codes
// (verified: `#[bg=blue,fg=black]` emits ESC[30m ESC[44m), which the
// terminal resolves from its own palette at DRAW time rather than at
// pane-creation time. Both ends of that path are already matugen-driven
// and already hot-reload: the `themes` block in zellij-config.kdl and
// kitty's ANSI palette. So the bar now re-themes live, with no restart.
//
// The trade, stated plainly: this bar can use only the theme's 8 named
// slots, not the full Material You role set. Mapping comes from
// zellij-config.kdl's own themes block —
//   blue=primary  yellow=secondary  green=tertiary  red=error
//   black=surface_variant  white=on_surface_variant
// Change a colour HERE by changing that mapping THERE, never by pasting
// a hex value back into this file — a hex value silently reverts this
// file to the non-live-reloading behaviour described above.
//
// ── Doubled-brace guard ───────────────────────────────────────────────
// Two opening braces must never appear adjacent in the rendered output —
// theme-parity scans every contract file raw for a doubled-brace template
// leftover and would fail the file. NOTE the extra hazard in this file
// that zellij-config.kdl does not have: zjstatus format strings use
// SINGLE-brace placeholders of their own ({session}, {mode}, {tabs}).
// Those are zjstatus syntax, not matugen syntax, and are correct as
// written — a single brace is passed through literally, verified against
// matugen 4.1.0 directly. Never place one immediately beside a matugen
// opening delimiter.
//
// AND NOTE, learned the hard way while writing this file: matugen parses
// this whole file, KDL comments included. It has no idea `//` means
// anything. A doubled opening brace written literally in a comment here —
// even inside backticks, as prose about the rule — opens an expression
// that never closes, and the parse error is then reported at whatever
// line the parser finally gives up on, NOT at the comment that caused it.
// That is why this paragraph describes the delimiter in words instead of
// quoting it. Do not "helpfully" add an example.
//
// ── KDL multi-line rule (D-07, inherited and still load-bearing) ──────
// An inline single-line child block is a PARSE ERROR in KDL — measured:
// `{ welcome_screen true }` on one line fails outright. Every child block
// below is therefore multi-line, one key per line. This is also what lets
// the contract's `kdl-plugin` extractor read one `name "value"` per line.
//
// NOTE ON THIS BEING A MATUGEN TEMPLATE AT ALL: since the switch to named
// colours, nothing in the plugin block interpolates — the rendered output
// is byte-identical for every palette. It is deliberately KEPT as a
// rendered contract target anyway, because that is what makes theme-doctor
// and theme-parity verify the file exists, is non-empty and is well-formed
// across all 22 themes (measured: 1897 passed / 0 failed with it static).
// The wiring also stays ready if a hex accent is ever wanted back.

layout {
    default_tab_template {
        pane size=1 borderless=true {
            plugin location="file:~/.config/zellij/plugins/zjstatus.wasm" {
                format_left "{mode}{tabs}"
                format_right "{command_git}{datetime}"
                format_space "#[bg=black]"
                format_hide_on_overlength "true"
                format_precedence "lrc"

                border_enabled "false"
                hide_frame_for_single_pane "false"

                mode_normal "#[bg=blue,fg=black,bold] NORMAL #[bg=black,fg=blue]"
                mode_locked "#[bg=red,fg=black,bold] LOCKED #[bg=black,fg=red]"
                mode_pane "#[bg=green,fg=black,bold] PANE #[bg=black,fg=green]"
                mode_tab "#[bg=yellow,fg=black,bold] TAB #[bg=black,fg=yellow]"
                mode_scroll "#[bg=yellow,fg=black,bold] SCROLL #[bg=black,fg=yellow]"
                mode_search "#[bg=yellow,fg=black,bold] SEARCH #[bg=black,fg=yellow]"
                mode_resize "#[bg=green,fg=black,bold] RESIZE #[bg=black,fg=green]"
                mode_move "#[bg=green,fg=black,bold] MOVE #[bg=black,fg=green]"
                mode_session "#[bg=blue,fg=black,bold] SESSION #[bg=black,fg=blue]"
                mode_prompt "#[bg=blue,fg=black,bold] PROMPT #[bg=black,fg=blue]"
                // NOTE: zellij ships one more mode, a compatibility mode
                // named after the multiplexer this repo retired, and
                // zjstatus has a styling slot for it. It is deliberately
                // NOT styled here, and not named here either. That mode
                // exists to ease migration FROM that surface, so styling
                // it would be dead weight AND would reintroduce the
                // surface's name into a file retirement-check scans as a
                // blocking class — which it correctly rejects. Unstyled,
                // the mode still works; it renders in zjstatus defaults.
                mode_default_to_mode "normal"

                tab_normal "#[bg=black,fg=white] {index} {name} "
                tab_active "#[bg=cyan,fg=black,bold] {index} {name} #[bg=black,fg=cyan]"
                tab_sync_indicator " "
                tab_fullscreen_indicator " "
                tab_floating_indicator " "

                command_git_command "git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD"
                command_git_format "#[bg=black,fg=green]#[bg=green,fg=black,bold]  {stdout} "
                command_git_interval "5"
                command_git_rendermode "static"

                datetime "#[bg=black,fg=white] {format} "
                datetime_format "%H:%M"
                datetime_timezone "Africa/Cairo"
            }
        }
        children
        // zellij's built-in keybind-hint bar, restored deliberately.
        //
        // The stock default layout is tab-bar (top) + status-bar (bottom),
        // and a default_tab_template REPLACES BOTH. zjstatus takes over the
        // tab-bar role at the top; without this pane the bottom keybind
        // hints simply vanish, which is a real loss of discoverability and
        // exactly what the config.kdl keybinds comment relies on when it
        // says zellij's defaults "are discoverable from the status bar
        // itself". One row, and it is themed by the same rendered `themes`
        // block in config.kdl, so it follows every palette like the rest.
        pane size=1 borderless=true {
            plugin location="status-bar"
        }
    }
}
